1 ok: weighted degree <= d => h -> v(h.J) is its own Taylor polynomial of order d
2 ok: only constant labels have Taylor data (c,0,...,0) at every jet
3 ok: x*y (weight 5) has zero Taylor data through order 4; the degree bound is needed
4 ok: V_0 and V_1 contain only constants; the remark is vacuous but true there
5 ok: D_t (factor count) is diagonal with nonzero entries; D_t of a nonconstant label is nonconstant
